diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d1adbd6..1cb6c36 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,6 +9,17 @@ Reminders use local Android notifications (permission is requested on Android 13
 Add Project tracker from the Android launcher’s widget picker and choose a project. Add the widget again for additional projects: each instance is configured independently. Widgets have a transparent background and update when project data changes. Project data stays on the device.
 
 ## Build
-Requires JDK 17, Android SDK 35 and Gradle 8.9. Run `gradle assembleDebug`. The resulting APK is debug-signed for personal use. GitHub Actions builds on pushes and publishes the APK on `v*` tags. Debug keys on CI may differ between builds; uninstalling an older build to install a new one removes its local data.
+Requires JDK 17, Android SDK 35 and Gradle 8.9. Run `gradle assembleRelease` for a signed,
+non-debuggable release APK at `app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk`, or
+`gradle assembleDebug` for a local debugging build.
+
+Release builds are signed with the committed key in `keystore/` (see `keystore/README.md`),
+so every release installs over the previous one. GitHub Actions runs `assembleRelease` on
+pushes and publishes `Progress-tracker-v<version>.apk` on `v*` tags, after verifying that the
+APK is release-signed and not debuggable.
+
+Releases up to and including v1.2.0 were debug-signed with a throwaway CI debug key. Because
+that signature can never match the release key, installing v1.2.1 or later over one of those
+builds needs a one-time uninstall, which also clears the app's local data.
 
 The browser preview in `preview/` is a separate interactive approximation, with separate browser storage; it is not the Android app or widget.
